--- a/public/guide.html
+++ b/public/guide.html
@@ -342,7 +342,7 @@
           <h3>Capture a world</h3>
           <p>Clear hostile fleets, then use the attack action while orbiting the enemy colony. Bombardment reduces its defenses and the colony returns fire. You capture it when defenses reach zero and your attacking fleet survives. Capturing reduces population by one, to a minimum of one, and cancels its construction project.</p>
           <p>The <strong>Invade</strong> preview shows the colony’s remaining defense, your damage range, expected retaliation, remaining hull, and whether capture is possible or guaranteed if you attack now. It explicitly warns when retaliation will destroy the formation; clearing all defenses does not capture a colony if the attacker is destroyed. The resulting report records actual defense damage, retaliation, and ownership. Each bombardment costs one order and one remaining move.</p>
-          <p>Base colony defense is 12 plus 3 per population. Original capital worlds add 15; an Orbital Bastion adds another 30. A colony recovers 5 defense each turn when no hostile fleet is in orbit, so maintaining pressure matters.</p>
+          <p>Base colony defense is 12 plus 3 per population. Original capital worlds add 15; an Orbital Bastion adds another 30. Bastions strengthen colony defense and retaliation against invasions; they do not fire on orbiting fleets or prevent a Beacon blockade. A colony recovers 5 defense each turn when no hostile fleet is in orbit, so maintaining pressure matters.</p>
           <h3>Repair and regroup</h3>
           <p>Each owned colony supplies a shared pool of <strong>4 hull repairs per cycle</strong>, or <strong>8 with an Orbital Shipyard</strong>, plus any Forge charter bonus. If no hostile fleet is present, its damaged fleets share that capacity in proportion to their missing hull. The system inspector previews each share. Splitting or merging at the same colony does not increase total recovery; dispersing between colonies gives access to their separate repair capacity. Emergency repairs still restore up to 24 hull immediately for 10 minerals and one order. Repairs cannot replace ships already destroyed.</p>
           <p>Coherent Lances improves damage by 25%, and Deflector Fields reduces incoming damage by 20%. Distributed Command gives warships a second move, allowing them to move and attack in the same turn when Orders permit.</p>
